※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4523

※ A result written `TYPE?` has an error that is the fact that there is no
※ answer and nothing more; one written `TYPE?ERROR` has an error that carries a
※ value.  Which of the two is being made is the type it is being made as, and a
※ value written for an error that has nowhere to put it is a value nothing
※ would ever read.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8? = ⊥ 7u16
